# Change Speed sends DO_CHANGE_SPEED with the box's number in param2, and the vehicle answers it.
#
# modifyandSetSpeed_Click: doCommandAsync(DO_CHANGE_SPEED, 0, (float) Value, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) - no
# unit conversion. A disarmed SITL copter refuses a speed of type 0, but it answers, and the answer
# in the message log is the proof the command arrived. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:4426-4438`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-changespeed.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 5

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

click fly-speed-value
key ctrl+u
type 7.5
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
click fly-changespeed
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_DO_CHANGE_SPEED 0,7.5,0,0,0,0,0
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_DO_CHANGE_SPEED:
